    distills: "DEC-16 — the design-file retirement order: distil the forks to docs/decisions/, verify the TSDoc block is complete, then remove. The distillation checklist's one T2 candidate, and shape-level because it constrains what W7 may build. What makes it a decision rather than plan detail: a ~600-line design file compiles to a nine-line TSDoc block and the difference is not padding — the fork cards and frame drivers have no home in code (CopyButton's D1 on label-swap vs chip vs toast; D2b's adjacency test), because code shows the choice and never the road not taken, and that is also the part nobody re-reads, which is why the file looks redundant once the component exists. Enforcement is W7's and must be a predicate, on DEC-15's own reasoning. Four rejected options recorded, including delete-alongside-the-build (fresh code, cold forks — the wrong moment) and keep-the-files-forever (two homes for one contract, the drift this epic exists to kill)"
